-- ==========================================================================
-- 78: RECOVERED -- findings that existed only in re_kb_data/ (the
-- gitignored RocksDB store) and in no committed file.
--
-- re_kb/README.md describes re_kb_data/ as "a rebuildable RocksDB store".
-- That was not true when this file was generated: these 24 curated
-- findings had no other home, so the documented rebuild procedure would
-- have silently destroyed them. Generated by _dump_live_only.py.
--
-- Review the statuses. These predate the promotion rule in
-- 77_epistemics.surql, so `confirmed` here means "someone wrote
-- confirmed", not "reproduction- or code-grade evidence is cited".
-- ==========================================================================
USE NS re DB kb;

UPSERT finding:body_walker_y_anchor SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-12',
  statement='BODY WALKER Y-ANCHOR — RESOLVED, code-derived, byte-exact (NO ground-truth pinning). CLOSED FORM (per body part, simple+scale path facing=0/flags=0): screenY = baseY + scaleY * (s16)(penY_acc + m*pitchY) ; where baseY = leaf_e460(node+0xE4) + scaleY*(s16)node[0x136]  (leaf_e460 = floor-toward-neg-inf via the ftrc/0x4b000000-magic leaf bank11 loc_8C11E460, called at loc_8c0344d4 entry on the node+0x104==0 path; node[0x136]=Y hotspot, =0 for this object); scaleY = node+0xF0 (=15/7 here); penY_acc = cumulative pen, Y-acc -= record.dy per record (finding:cumulative_pen_geometry); m*pitchY = the per-TILE tile-height term = r5 = A*desc[3] - slot20  (A=m=descriptor byte0, desc[3]=pitchY, slot20=0 unless 0x4000 X-mirror), computed in loc_8c03478e. The walker\'s screenY (logged at PC 0x8C034864) is the part\'s BOTTOM-LEFT anchor (MVC2 bottom-up tile anchoring); the engine submit loc_8c1244b0 lays the TA quad UPWARD so vertex A(top-left).Y = screenY - tileHeight, D(bottom-left).Y = screenY (CONFIRMED: engine TA sprite maxY == ASMTRACE screenY, 0.004px). ROOT CAUSE of the old +tile_height*scaleY-per-record error: the harness build_image_dump.py fabricated baseY by a regression that integerized (sY-baseY)/scaleY (snapped to floor(node+0xE4)=333) AND zeroed node+0x136 — the integer-index solve aliased the true origin by exactly m*pitchY*scaleY (the dominant tile term). gen_walker.c (the transpiled walker) was ALREADY byte-exact; the fix was purely (a) feed the REAL f32 node+0xE0/E4/EC/F0 + real node+0x134/0x136 from the RAM dump and let the walker\'s own leaf_e460 floor + hotspot fmac derive the origin (no regression), and (b) lay TA corners upward in test_ta_emit.c to match the engine\'s bottom-anchor convention. VALIDATION (raw walker, NO external Y-fix): per-part screenY vs ASMTRACE _ryu_capture/asm_angled_fist.log cid23 frame10766 = MAX dX 0.0033px / dY 0.0043px (within the trace\'s 0.01px log quantization); converge_byte_exact.mjs = 9/9 corners byte-exact vs the engine\'s own TA (mc_engine_ta.bin) 0.0000px; render+pixel-diff (render_ta.mjs -> diff_png.mjs) RAW ta_walker.bin vs engine GT = 100.0000% / 0 diff px / maxΔ=0. CITE: marvelous2 bank03 loc_8c0344d4 (10271-10314 hotspot fmac origin; 10616-10683 per-tile m*pitch; entry leaf floor) + bank11 loc_8C11E460 (floor leaf) + bank12 loc_8c1244b0 (TA submit/quad layout). Tools: tools/render-replica-poc/{gen_walker.c (unchanged), build_image_dump.py, test_ta_emit.c, converge_byte_exact.mjs}.',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:bug_rocket_emitter_far_heuristic SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-11',
  statement='BUG A (Sentinel LP rocket-punch wrong direction): the EMITTER client path buildEmitterDrawList (sprite-client.mjs ~2045-2074) still uses the OLD far>130 owner-anchor heuristic + conditional facing (objFacing = (far && ownFlip) ? o.xflip : osl.facing), whereas the WHOLE-SPRITE path buildDrawList (~1140-1257) was already fixed to px=o.x,py=o.y unconditional + fl=o.xflip!==sp.facing. The rocket projectile screen pos (its own diagonal-down arc) IS on the wire at OBJS x/y = node+0xE0/E4 (loc_8c030af8 CONFIRMED), but the emitter ignores it while the fist is < 130px from Sentinel, anchoring to the owner instead -> projectile draws horizontal/displaced, not down-forward. v86 guess (use o.xflip) did not fix it because (1) the gate is far which is false early and (2) facing was not the dominant error. ROOT CAUSE = client emitter path NOT using the projectile own screen_xy; FIX = match buildDrawList: px=o.x,py=o.y unconditional and objFacing from o.xflip unconditional (no far gate).',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:emitter_audit_2026_06_10 SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-10',
  resolved_item3='RESOLVED 2026-06-10 (finding:emitter_limb_placement): MISSING item (3) offline-vs-live selector reconciliation / ~3pct residual was the STORAGE-vs-LOGICAL part crop. GFX1 header [lw][lh][sw][sh]; engine draws lw*8 x lh*8 bottom-left LOGICAL region at full CPS, extractor packed full sw*8 x sh*8 storage -> padded limbs 2x oversized + pen-offset. Fixed in extract_gfx1_atlas.py (crop bottom-left logical), PL00 re-baked + deployed. The ~3pct X residual on sid64 in emitter_scale_derived also traces to this (storage padding), not a CPS error. P4 \'upright bake\' band-aid (emitFlipY) still stands separately.',
  statement='OFF-SH4 EMITTER PIPELINE AUDIT (2026-06-10). DEDUP VERDICT: the project ALREADY has a zero-raster path to unify — buildEmitterLiveCharq() (sprite-client.mjs:1326) emits the EXACT PVR2Renderer _charqParsed contract (28-byte verts + op/pt/tr PolyParam) and renders through pvr2-renderer.mjs (renderCharq, webgpu-test.html:471), identical to CHARQ + the green DIFF. It is GATED OFF (window._emitterLive=false) on ONE open blocker: the offline sel->TCW (live VRAM tile address) mapping is unsolved (heuristicSelToTcw is a guess). The SHIPPING path is buildEmitterDrawList -> sprite-gpu.mjs (SpriteGPU.render), a SEPARATE 2D quad rasterizer. So TWO rasterizers exist. RECOMMENDATION: do NOT delete sprite-gpu yet — it is the only path that works TODAY because it samples a pre-baked RGB/indexed atlas (no TCW needed). Unify by solving sel->TCW (Oracle probe @0x8C0345C4 dumping r11 VRAM base + resulting TCW, per buildEmitterLiveCharq doc), lighting up buildEmitterLiveCharq, and retiring sprite-gpu\'s char path — leaving sprite-gpu ONLY for the hit-spark/effect additive passes pvr2 doesn\'t cover. DUPLICATION: textured-quad raster, UV mirror (flip/flipY), additive blend, palette recolor all exist in BOTH; sprite-gpu UNIQUELY does the 128-color palette-LUT recolor + skin override + idx-atlas LUT (pvr2 gets recolor for free via live PVR palette RAM). MISSING: (1) sel->TCW mapping = the unify blocker; (2) offline emitter atlas exists for ONLY 1 char (PL2A Storm deployed, not the full 59) vs 60 whole-sprite atlases; (3) offline-vs-live selector reconciliation gap (sid64 torso 64px offline vs 128px live) = ~3pct X residual + possible wrong sels — rip_gfx2_assembly read_cells walks cell==sprite_id correctly but the part DIMS/scale differ; (4) no atlas/effects dir built — effects bank (Effect Poly 0x0CED0000, resolve-by-GFX-pointer) unhandled offline, relies on streamed STAF/EFCT; (5) no _idx.png/_lut.json deployed so live-skin LUT path is dormant. ADD: skins (setSkin/setCharLUT path coded but 0 LUT atlases built); effects atlas by GFX-type. TWEAK: _emitFlipY render-time global Y-flip is a band-aid for a bottom-up atlas bake (KB emitter_y_axis_fix) — clean fix = bake upright in extract_gfx1_atlas.py, keep only FLAGS&0x8000; deferred for regression risk but cheap once roster re-bake happens. WIRE: enrich fields ARE shipped (scaleX/Y@0x50/54, pal12d/12e@0x12d/12e, overlay1a4@0x1a4, GSTA 49-byte stride) and consumed client-side (sprite-client.mjs:846); hit-flash/overlay are APPROXIMATE additive tints not exact bank-swap (loc_8c035162). PRIORITY by pixel-fidelity: P1 sel->TCW unify (kills the dual-rasterizer + the ~3pct residual at once), P2 roster bake-out (1->59), P3 selector-dim reconciliation, P4 upright bake, P5 effects atlas, P6 skins LUT.',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:emitter_facing_dump_tool SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-11',
  statement='DUMP-FRAME TOOL added (webgpu-test.html v=78, sprite-client.mjs gated window._emitDumpReq; deployed 149.28.44.118 sprite-client md5 3ea12bcf / webgpu-test md5 e578353e). Exports per-frame JSON for BOTH on-screen chars: gsta{facing,screen_x,screen_y,cid,slot,sid} + TA-TRUTH per-part quads (from window._lastParsed opaque/pt/tr lists, z>=reCut foreground, bbox x,y,w,h,cx,cy = the green DIFF ground truth, grouped per-player by nearest anchorX) + EMITTER per-part quads (sel,x,y,w,h,flip,posReflect in game-space 640x480) + taExtent/emitterExtent leftReach/rightReach from anchor. PURPOSE: derive facing numerically, not by eyeball A/B. V77-vs-V76 FUNCTIONAL DIFF (the ONLY code change, all else comment-only): faceInv default TRUE to FALSE; bodyFace replaced by single sense F = (faceInv? !facing : facing) XOR faceFlip, with posReflect = F and flip = F XOR r.flip — so faceFlip now wholesale-inverts BOTH transforms together. RESULT: reachable toggle space collapsed to 2 states (F or !F); POSITION reflect and TEXTURE-U mirror are RIGIDLY coupled and can never take opposite senses. Operator reports neither state makes both players correct => PROVES position and texture need INDEPENDENT polarity (one of the two JS transforms is inverted relative to the engine). The dump derives WHICH from the numbers: TA-truth leftReach vs rightReach per char = the real facing direction; compared to emitterExtent + the facing byte it yields the facing-byte to screen-direction map and whether posReflect and flip each need facing or !facing.',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:emitter_roster_deploy_2026_06_10 SET
  date='2026-06-10',
  fix_404_storm='negative-cache _asmMissing Set (deployed v=67): attempt once per char_id, on 404 add cid and skip every frame; resetAsmMissing re-arms after a deploy. Stops the per-frame Date.now refetch storm.',
  id_str='emitter_roster_deploy_2026_06_10',
  in_match='7=PL07 Wolverine, 19=PL13 RubyHeart, 1=PL01 Zangief, 38=PL26 Bison, 45=PL2D Shuma, 48=PL30 OmegaRed, 10=PL0A Rogue, 13=PL0D Hulk, 14=PL0E Venom, 42=PL2A Storm, 23=PL17 Cable; all renderable now',
  mapping='char_id to PLxx = RAW 2-digit uppercase hex, NO lookup table. sprite-client.mjs:693 loadAsmChar hex=(cid and 0xff).toString(16).padStart(2).toUpperCase(). Verified vs KB roster 0x00 to 0x3A and char23=PL17 Cable, char42=PL2A Storm.',
  status='RESOLVED',
  summary='All 59 PLxx emitter atlases (parts.png/parts.json/asm.json + idx.png/lut.json) extracted FULLY OFFLINE from dasm_PLDAT/Output via tools/extract_gfx1_atlas.py (GFX1 LZSS loc_8c0354c0 + PVR PAL4 detwiddle + GFX2 cumulative-pen). 0 decode failures, 100 percent PAL4. Deployed scp-only to 149.28.44.118 test-atlas/chars/ (backup chars-backup-20260610-214949). Prod 59/59 asm.json, all HTTP-200.',
  title='Full 59-char emitter atlas roster extracted + deployed to prod';

UPSERT finding:emitter_tile_scale_charq_calibrated SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-10',
  files='["web/webgpu/sprite-client.mjs:buildEmitterDrawList", "web/webgpu-test.html?v=68"]',
  source='CHARQ _ryu_capture/chosen_body.json (sid64 scale[1,1]); operator DIFF-overlay frames _emframes/f_03,06,07; deploy md5 abb9667d sprite-client.mjs v=68',
  statement='EMITTER selKeyed (offline GFX1-detwiddle atlas) part-extent + flip calibrated to CHARQ ground truth. SIZE: the offline atlas emits BOTH the cumulative pen (r.dx/r.dy) AND the part pixels at 2x the cell grid (1 pen cell-unit = 2 native px), so the WHOLE assembly shares ONE scale native->screen = CPS/2 = (5/3/2, 15/7/2) = (0.833, 1.071). Proof: CHARQ chosen_body.json scale[1,1] a 128x128 body tile renders to 106x137 screen px = CPS/2 within 0.3pct; sid64 full-assembly bbox at CPS/2 ~ 67x137 ~= GT 146 tall. OLD bug: pen used full CPS (pcX/pcY) while tile used only live-zoom (cpsx~1) = two different scales -> skeleton spread 2x wider than tiles -> fragmented/small body (operator Size slider ~1.75x was hand-undoing the missing X CPS). FIX (sprite-client.mjs buildEmitterDrawList selKeyed branch ~1548): pen AND tile AND ax/ay all use tsX/tsY = (CPS*tileScale)*zoom, tileScale default 0.5, exposed as window._asmCfg.tileScale. FLIP: the cumulative-pen rip is FACING-NEUTRAL (rip_gfx2_assembly.py:177 X-acc += dx, no sign flip) baking ONE branch of (X-acc +/-dx by facing@0x110); frames proved that branch is OPPOSITE the raw owner.facing byte (live Ryu faced right yet emitter mirrored him). FIX: flip = (faceInv ? !owner.facing : !!owner.facing) XOR r.flip, faceInv default true (window._emitFaceInv). r.flip (per-part 0x4000 X-mirror) still XORs on top.',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:gsta_draw_layer_per_slot SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-11',
  statement='GSTA needs a per-body-slot draw_layer byte for EXACT z-order. The TRUE MVC2 draw order is the on-screen slot/LAYER table (count u8 @ 0x8C2895E0[layer], ptr u32 @ 0x8C287DE0 + layer*0x180 + i*4, 16 layers, walked by render-list loc_8c0308c2). The 6 fighter BODY nodes (CHAR_BASE P1C1..P2C3) are present IN this slot table (readAllDrawn skips them via the isBody==CHAR_BASE[s] check, gamestate.cpp:393), so each body\'s authoritative z-rank = the LAYER index whose 0x8C287DE0 pointer array contains CHAR_BASE[s]. DERIVATION (producer, read-only): for s in 0..5: for layer in 0..15: count=read8(0x8C2895E0+layer); for i in 0..count-1: if read32(0x8C287DE0+layer*0x180+i*4)==CHAR_BASE[s] then draw_layer[s]=layer. Ship 1 byte/char draw_layer (default 0xFF if not found in any layer that frame = inactive/offscreen). This is the SAME field OBJS already carries as o.type (set out[n].type=layer at gamestate.cpp:416); body slots simply lacked it because readGameState never walked the slot table. Client buildDrawList currently falls back to char_id / screen_y-depth (sprite-client.mjs ~1995-2014, window._emitZByDepth stopgap) which is wrong on P1-behind-P2 overlap; with draw_layer the client sorts char GROUPS by layer (lower layer = drawn first = behind) exactly like the engine. CONFIRMED: slot-table layout (reference_mvc2_slot_table_drawlist + gamestate.cpp readAllDrawn), body-in-slot-table (the isBody skip), o.type=layer mapping (serializeObjects:697). The per-slot WALK to find each body\'s layer is the new derivation here.',
  status='confirmed',
  tags='["contribution_candidate", "gsta_wire", "z_order"]';

UPSERT finding:gsta_sprite_id_sampling_phase SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-11',
  statement='ROOT CAUSE of \'wrong sprite during fast moves\' (Sentinel rocket 213/214 vs diagonal 428-430; Storm dash; electric arc) = GSTA sprite_id SAMPLING PHASE, not a wrong field/atlas. The body walker loc_8c0344d4 (bank03:10232-10243) reads char+0x144 masked &0x7FFF (loc_8c0345fc=0x160, add 0xE4 imm8 sign-ext -0x1C => 0x144; loc_8c0345fe=0x7fff) the SAME engine phase it is written. char+0x144 is written by the anim tick loc_8c034dee (bank03:11567): decrements anim_timer@0x142 (add 0xFF), and ON expiry advances current_cell@0x154 by +0x14 (20B keyframe) and duff-copies (bank12.loc_8c1294c8, mov 0x14,r0) the 20B keyframe from deref(0x154) into player+0x140, so +0x144 = keyframe[4] = deref(0x154)+4. Engine ground-truth (Oracle mc_oracle_charPassCapture at rend_start_render Renderer_if.cpp:649, reads +0x144 at the STARTRENDER moment = same phase as loc_8c0344d4): _ryu_capture/oracle_hook_20260611.jsonl node 0x0C2688E4 (Sentinel cid23) cycles 213(178491)>214(178494)>428(178499)>429(178501)>430(178504)>215(178507); diagonal 428-430 spans ~6 frames 178499-178504. The wire (GSTA) samples +0x144 via readGameState in serverPublish at render()/DequeueRender (mirror.cpp:2323), which lags the engine render phase by ~1 frame under threaded rendering + MVC2 multi-pass STARTRENDER (QueueRender single-slot DROPS the character pass; only the HUD/composite pass survives to render(), Renderer_if.cpp:634-651). The \'ASSEMBLY RE-KEY\' read read16(cellP+4) is NOT fresher (gamestate.cpp:1169-1170 own comment: keyframe[4]==sid144). FIX = move the GSTA readGameState sample EARLIER, into rend_start_render alongside mc_oracle_charPassCapture (the STARTRENDER/character-pass phase where loc_8c0344d4 ran), OR latch sprite_id (+0x144) and anim_timer (+0x142) into a render-phase snapshot in mc_oracle_charPassCapture and have readGameState ship the latched value. Same lag affects OBJS satellites: readAllDrawn (gamestate.cpp:381) reads node+0x144 (line 406). Read-only, determinism-safe (no guest writes).',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:gsta_wire_ext_completeness_2026_06_11 SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-11',
  statement='GSTA WIRE EXT COMPLETENESS AUDIT (2026-06-11, READ-ONLY). PART A (correctness) = SIGN-OFF. (1) draw_layer slot-table walk is byte-exact vs Render_sprites loc_8c0308c2 (bank03:1200): 16 layers, count u8@0x8C2895E0+L (loop end r8=base+0x10), node ptrs u32@0x8C287DE0+L*0x180+i*4, node base absolute; outer loop iterates layers 0->15 ASCENDING => lower layer = drawn first = behind (client ASCENDING-sort is correct); 0xFF sentinel + cnt>0x60 guard are safe additions (disasm has no clamp, trusts count). Bodies ARE in the arrays (readAllDrawn excludes them by base-match). (2) All new offsets are byte/right-width per pl_mem.asm: 0x1D2 xflip, 0x1F9 stance, 0x201 Flight_Flag, 0x202 Buff_HyperArmor (all #symbol byte); 0x025 pl_palid_match (byte); 0x151 RenderExtra has NO pl_mem symbol but IS cell byte+0x11 bulk-copied into player+0x140..0x153 by anim tick loc_8c034dee (literal 0x0140, r0=0x14=20B copy) => valid. NUANCE: the render body walker loc_8c0344d4 gates facing on char+0x110 (literal 0x0110 @loc_8c034606), NOT 0x1D2 -- shipping BOTH 0x110(facing_right) and 0x1D2(facing_1d2) is correct; client should prefer 0x110 for byte-faithful render, 0x1D2 only to pre-empt turn-around lag. (3) effect_key=low16(node+0x15C) is a stable discriminator WITHIN the 64KB Effect Poly bank [0x0CED0000,0x0CEE0000) (bank base stage-loaded once, not per-frame churned); effect TYPE (OBJS type byte) remains the primary routing key. serialize/deserialize symmetric (C++ + JS 57B stride + OBJS stride-13 autodetect). PART B (completeness for pixel-perfect): the gfx2_cell body record is 8B [dx][dy][FLAGS][sel] with FLAGS consumed ONLY for 0x4000 X-mirror / 0x8000 Y-mirror (loc_8c0347bc/0x0347c8) => bodies carry NO per-part blend/alpha/palette; bodies are uniformly Dat_Pal + opaque/punch-through, so no per-part override is missing. REMAINING GAPS (not folded yet): (G1 ASSET) Effect Poly 0x0CED0000 textures not yet ripped to effects.json -> effects render blank; (G2 STATE) per-object BLEND mode for effects/supers/auras is NOT on GSTA -- effects ride OBJS sprite_id/screen and need an additive-vs-alpha bit; carried correctly only on the STAF/HUDF->pvr2-renderer path (tsp bits), NOT on the lean OBJS path; (G3 STATE) global super-flash / screen-flash whole-frame tint is a separate engine mechanism, not a per-char field -- needs its own global byte if faithful; (G4) hurt-flash base = pl_palid_match@0x25 (+0x300 hurt offset, loc_8c035000) NOW shipped (pal_color_25) + 0x12e(pal_12e)/0x1a4(overlay_1a4) handler-dispatch fields shipped => flash/tint CLOSED on the wire, pending client wiring. bit15 of sprite_id = transform-variant (loc_8c0348c8 vs loc_8c0344d4 via caller loc_8c034bea) -- shipped raw, client masks &0x7FFF + carries sid_xform (sprite-client.mjs:840). VERDICT: the 7 added bytes are correct and sufficient for BODY pixel-perfect; the only true wire GAP for full-scene pixel-perfect is a per-effect BLEND byte on OBJS (G2) -- fold a 1-byte blend/list-type into the OBJS effect record in THIS pass. Everything else is asset (G1) or a separate global (G3, defer).',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:gsta_wire_field_audit SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-11',
  statement='GSTA WIRE FIELD AUDIT — definitive gap list for full-fidelity off-SH4 render, derived from the render-path READS (not guessed). BASELINE SHIPPED (verified maplecast_gamestate.cpp readGameState ~1961-1984 + .h WIRE_SIZE=328, stride 49/char): GSTA per-char = active@0x0, char_id@0x1, facing(from 0x110 copy), health@0x420, red_health@0x424, special_move(from 0x1E9), assist(0x4C9), palette(from 0x52D), pos_x/y@0x34/38, screen_x/y@0xE0/E4, vel_x/y, sprite_id@0x144, anim_state@0x1D0, anim_timer@0x142, anim_ptr@0x168, AND the GSTA-enrich already-landed: scale_x/y@0x50/0x54, pal_12d@0x12D, pal_12e@0x12E, overlay_1a4@0x1A4. PALF ships char+0x40. OBJS/OBJF ships pool nodes (owner_cid, sprite_id@0x12C, screen@0xC8/CC or 0xE0/E4, type, category@0x3, xflip@0x130, is_effect=node+0x15C in [0x0CED0000,0x0CEE0000), hot_dx/dy from node+0x178). So spec-§6 gaps #1(scale) #2(pal 12d/12e) are CLOSED; effect-routing tag is_effect is SHIPPED.
REMAINING GAPS (drives a visual, NOT on wire), priority order:
[P1 CORRECTNESS, not a new field] sprite_id SAMPLING PHASE — char+0x144 is WRITTEN by anim tick loc_8c034dee (bank03:11567, copies cell+4 to +0x144) and CONSUMED same-frame by body walker loc_8c0344d4. readGameState must sample +0x144 (and 0x142 anim_timer, 0x12e) AFTER the SH4 has run the frame\'s anim tick (serverPublish at vblank end), else the body renders one frame stale = the Ryu defect. CONFIRMED (loc_8c034dee writer / loc_8c0344d4 reader).
[P1] char+0x151 RenderExtra (u8) — additive super/aura/overlay CLASS (Storm 12=Lightning Storm,13=Hailstorm,39=Lightning Attack,64=flight aura). Copied by anim tick loc_8c034dee (bank03:11567 / re-catalog 00-README:117). NOTE: enrich shipped 0x1A4 (runtime handler-dispatch source, loc_8c035254) but NOT 0x151 (the per-cell RenderExtra). Both feed overlay selection; 0x151 is the cell-authoritative one. Without it: supers/auras/electric overlays cannot be selected. CONFIRMED.
[P2] facing SOURCE — wire reads 0x110 (xflip COPY); authoritative is 0x1D2 (pl_mem:147). 0x110 lags 0x1D2 during a turn-around frame. Body walker loc_8c0344d4 gates on 0x110 in the render copy, but SETTER loc_8c0d97ee writes 0x110 from pos compare; the stable source is 0x1D2. FIX = read 0x1D2 (or both). Visual: 1-frame wrong-facing flicker on cross-up/turn. CONFIRMED.
[P2] palette SOURCE — wire ships palette_id from 0x52D (a DUPLICATE); the displayed-palette + flash-base index the palette path reads is pl_palid_match@0x25 (loc_8c035000 bank03:11891 reads 0x25, adds +0x300 hurt offset). 0x025 (OFF_COLOR) is defined but only used in the ptrdump probe, NOT serialized. FIX = ship 0x25. Visual: wrong color variant / missing hurt-bank flash base. CONFIRMED.
[P3] char+0x202 Buff_HyperArmor (u8) — armored-super body glow via palette path (loc_8c035000 char_id-branch; Zangief/SonSon special bank). Without it: missing armor glow on hyper-armor supers. CONFIRMED offset, INFERRED visual coupling.
[P3] char+0x201 Flight_Flag (u8) — flight stance/aura toggle, pairs with RenderExtra=64 (Storm/Magneto). Without it: flight aura overlay not gated. INFERRED (pl_mem:214 + PL2A-storm).
[P3] char+0x1F9 stance (u8) — stand/crouch/jump/otg; fixes the 2 unstable crouch crops. Cheap. INFERRED (pl_mem:191).
[P4 ASSET, not state] Effect Poly textures (0x0CED0000) not yet ripped → effects.json; per-char sprite scale population (which chars dynamically zoom) uncharacterized; world z@0x3C unneeded (transform done server-side, screen_x/y shipped).
SHIP-FOR-FIDELITY ORDER: (1) fix sprite_id/anim sampling phase [correctness], (2) +0x151 RenderExtra, (3) read facing from 0x1D2, (4) read palette from 0x25, (5) +0x202 HyperArmor, (6) +0x201 Flight, (7) +0x1F9 stance. Items 2/5/6/7 = +4 bytes/char wire bump; touches all 4 parsers per CLAUDE.md.',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:render_calltree_scope SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-12',
  statement='The MVC2 per-frame RENDER call-tree (root loc_8c0308c2 Render_sprites slot-walk; loc_8c0305d8 is a sibling setup entry) is BOUNDED: 114 functions / 842 basic blocks / ~9850 SH4 instructions across banks 02/03/11/12/13/17 = ~3% of the game. 85 distinct opcodes; FPU-heavy (ftrv x20 = the world->screen matrix*vec transform core in bank12 loc_8c1216c0/loc_8c1219b0; frchg x12 + fschg x22 = FPSCR.FR/SZ bank+size state MUST be modeled; fsca x3 sin/cos table; fmac x14). SINGLE-PRECISION throughout (1 isolated fcnvsd). ZERO privileged/MMU/trap/SMC/MMIO instructions (no trapa/sleep/ldtlb/movca/ldc/rte/fipr/fmtrx) -- clean user-mode FP+integer. INDIRECT BRANCHES ~96% statically resolved: 253 jsr/jmp via ROM pool constants (trivial def-use), 2 enumerable ROM jump tables (the cell-processor Duff device loc_8c1295bc=loc_8c12951c with 17 targets bounds-checked cmp/hs 0x40; the render-mode braf_8c0310ac switch with 8 targets), and only 1 TRUE RAM vtable (loc_8c0305ce: jmp @[obj+0x28], a per-object render-override method ptr; ~5 store sites in bank03; handle via one-site switch(pc) escape hatch). No general indirect-jump resolver needed. CORRECTION to a prior plan assumption: the bank11/bank12 leaf bodies (loc_8c1216c0, loc_8c11e2e0/e460/e860, loc_8c1244b0) are PRESENT in the marvelous2 checkout (earlier greps missed UPPERCASE loc_8C... labels) -- ZERO functions referenced-but-missing. The GFX1 LZSS/part decoder loc_8c033d78 is NOT in the render tree (load-time only) so the AOT tree auto-excludes it.',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:render_replica_byte_exact_proven SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-12',
  statement='BYTE-EXACT PIXEL REPRODUCTION PROVEN (2026-06-12, capstone). The transpiled render (lift-to-C: body walker loc_8c0344d4 + transform-product-read + submit loc_8c1244b0, geometry 0.00px + TCW/TSP bit-exact per finding:submit_tcw_resident) renders pixels BYTE-IDENTICAL to the engine\'s OWN TA through the same gold-standard pvr2-renderer (WebGPU): 100.0000% match = 307200/307200 px, maxΔ=0, meanΔ=0, over the validated object region. Validated from a SINGLE ALIGNED FRAME captured atomically on prod (RAM+VRAM+PVR+engine-TA at one render frame, via the MAPLECAST_DUMP_RAM one-shot in maplecast_oracle_hook.cpp charPassCapture = STARTRENDER: mem_b 16MB, vram 8MB, pvr_regs 32KB, ctx->tad.thd_root engine TA). Test object = P2C1 slot1, char_id=23 (Cable), sprite_id=212, sels {1264,1265,1266,1267} fmt5/pal28, texaddrs 0x61A720/7A0/800/880, node+0xDC=0 (descriptors at 0x8C1F9F9C base). Tooling: tools/render-replica-poc/ (build_image_dump.py reads THIS dump\'s resident control words + descriptors; test_ta_emit.c walker->transform->submit->ta_buffer.bin; render_ta.mjs headless ta-parser->pvr2-renderer->PNG; converge_byte_exact.mjs the proof). The captured frame was a mid-spawn/translucent intro instant so the opaque validated region is a small Cable fragment; the geometry/param/texel chain is byte-exact over it; a fully-on-screen frame exercises more texels, same proof. Two open/fixed items: (1) finding:body_walker_y_anchor (the one Y-origin term, pinned by the engine TA, to be derived from disasm); (2) finding:submit_isp_depthmode (resident ISP=0 -> renderer skips; engine finalizes DepthMode=4).',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:render_replica_option_c_validated SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-12',
  statement='OPTION C PROVEN (PoC GO, 2026-06-12, commit 050c4a01b, tools/render-replica-poc/). A lift-to-C transpiler (lift.py parse + codegen.py ~45-opcode table harvested from flycast core/hw/sh4/interpr/sh4_opcodes.cpp + emit_func.py delay-slot-aware control flow) mechanically translates MVC2\'s real per-frame body-render SH4 -> native C, bit-exact. RESULTS: leaf loc_8c11e460 (bank11 vertex builder, 24 insns) = 21/21 BIT-EXACT; transform core loc_8c0347c8..loc_8c034864 (per-tile FP+integer screen math) = 18/18 BIT-EXACT X+Y (scaleX=5/3 baseX=533, scaleY=15/7 baseY=116.57, residual 0.000px, within ASMTRACE\'s own 0.01px log quantization); full walker loc_8c0344d4 (464 insns/20 BBs, both paths, all loops+4 leaf-dispatch sites) compiles/runs/balanced-stack (r15 delta=0). FP-EXACTNESS RISK CLOSED: straight C float is bit-exact for the +/-/* transform chain (compiled /fp:precise, RM=0, single precision throughout per the §8 opcode analysis). The ONE opcode needing special-casing = fmac -> std::fmaf (fused, single rounding; flycast sh4_fpu.cpp:559; naive fr0*frm+frn rounds twice and diverges; 5 sites in the walker). Integer subtleties handled: 8-bit imm sign-ext (load-bearing: add 0xE4,r0 = +(-28) derives node+0x144 sprite_id from node+0x160), sign-ext mov.w/mov.b loads, ftrc 0x7fffff80 overflow clamp, exts.w before float, muls.w 16x16->32. GROUND TRUTH = _ryu_capture/asm_angled_fist.log (ASMTRACE logs loc_8c0344d4\'s per-part screenX/screenY AT PC 0x8C034864 = the exact output of the transpiled fn). OPEN: full NUMERIC walker run needs the 0x8C1F9F9C tile-descriptor table (load-time built, NOT on disc) + GFX1 part-dim bytes from a 16MB RAM dump (absent from repo) -- a one-time Oracle memcpy of those static regions closes it. Lifter GENERALIZES to the full 9850-insn tree: add ftrv/frchg/fsca/fschg, wire the 2 ROM jump tables + 1 RAM vtable as switches, transpile trig leaves loc_8c11e2e0/e860 + bank12 submit.',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:render_replica_phase1_codederived SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-12',
  note='OPEN-SEAM (a) [per-frame submit RECORD-ALLOCATION base cursor] is RESOLVED by finding:render_replica_phase2_slotwalk (2026-06-12): the base is computed by running the engines own allocation cursor -- arena 0x8C1F9D94 + node+0xDC prefix-sum (0x8C1F9D98), validated computed-prefix==resident node+0xDC + synthetic 2-body. Seam (b) loc_8C1216C0 proj-matrix SETUP still stubbed (camera matrices read resident).',
  statement='RENDER-REPLICA PHASE 1 DONE (2026-06-12, branch feat/render-replica-experiment, tools/render-replica-poc/). The per-object body render is now FULLY CODE-DERIVED -- the per-frame deposited state that was previously READ from the snapshot / pinned to the engine TA is COMPUTED. Three deposits transpiled + validated byte-exact vs the engine\'s OWN deposited values, ZERO engine-TA reads: (1) ANCHOR node+0xE0/E4 = the world->screen transform loc_8C122560 (bank12): ftrv of the composed XMTRX over node pos (0x34/38/3C) + perspective divide (inv=1/fv[3]; x*=inv; y*=inv). The composed XMTRX = M1.M2 where M1=viewport matrix @0x8C2D6B18, M2=projection @0x8C2D6AD8 -- FRAME-GLOBAL camera matrices (built once/frame by loc_8C1216C0, the proj-setup loc_8c03093c calls FIRST at bank03:1295 with fr4=640/fr5=480), legitimately resident (camera, not this object\'s render output). Reproduced node+0xE0=533.85986/node+0xE4=333.38766 byte-exact (engine 533.85986/333.38763, within f32 ULP). gen_transform_obj.c (hand-verified faithful port: load_mat + column-major ftrv matching codegen.py + matmul_colmaj M1.M2 + perspective divide; cites loc_8c120950 load / loc_8c120540 matmul / loc_8c11F870 ftrv / loc_8C122560 divide). (2) SCALE node+0xEC/F0 = loc_8c03093c (bank03:1336-1381): first scaleX = CpsXScale*node[0x50], scaleY = CpsYScale*node[0x54] (CpsXScale=0x3fd55555=5/3, CpsYScale=0x40092492=15/7, IMMEDIATES, work.asm:44-45), THEN divided by (0x444b16de / camZ) where camZ=*(0x8c26a538)=*(0x8c26a518+0x20)=812.357 (bank03:1369-1381). Final scaleX=1.666667/scaleY=2.142858 byte-exact. Transpiled via gen_render_object.py (loc_8c03093c, 180 insns, the jsr to loc_8c122560 routed to transform_object_122560). (3) TEXTURE PARAMS PCW/ISP/TSP/TCW = the submit finalize loc_8C1244B0 + loc_8C124910/124a82: read the RESIDENT 0x20-byte poly-param template rectab[idxtab[*rec]] (rectab=*(0x8C2DAD4c), idxtab=*(0x8C2DAD3c)), then finalize: PCW=(P&0xF8FCFFFF)|0x02000000 (loc_8c1246b0/124720); ISP=(I&0x1FFFFFFF)|(4<<29)=0x80000000 (DepthMode 4, loc_8c12467a); TSP=(T&0x03278FFF)|(((*(0x8C2AA4C4)^0xFC)<<24)|0x00100000|0x00800000)=0x949004D2 (loc_8c1246b0/124708); TCW=(T&0xF81FFFFF)|(palbank<<21) PalSelect inject (loc_8c124a82, palbank=24 = P2C1 slot formula 16*(0+1)+8*1). gen_submit_params.c. ALL 9 body tiles PCW/ISP/TSP/TCW byte-exact vs engine TA (test_render_object_full.exe). VALIDATION (cid23/P2C1 Cable sid212, frame10766, 9 body tiles): computed anchor/scale/params == engine\'s actual deposited values byte-exact; full pipeline render_object_setup_03093c -> transform -> walker(loc_8c0344d4, 9 tiles) -> submit_params -> sprite TA assembled with computed params+corners+UV == engine TA 864/864 sprite bytes IDENTICAL; rendered through the gold-standard pvr2-renderer (WebGPU) = 100.0000% pixel match (307200/307200, 0 diff px, maxΔ=0) vs the engine\'s own TA. NO PINNING: nothing read from mc_engine_ta.bin for any load-bearing field. SUPERSEDES the engine-TA-pinned texture-binding of finding:render_replica_byte_exact_proven (which kept the engine TA\'s param block). OPEN/transient seams honestly flagged: (a) the per-frame submit RECORD-ALLOCATION base index (rec_index 16..24 -> rectab[9..17]) is transient submit state, already consumed/reset (0x8C2DEE54=0) at the STARTRENDER dump instant; for THIS object it is RAM-DISCOVERABLE (the unique contiguous run of >=ntile pal24/fmt5 rectab entries == base 9) but the general per-frame cursor is not resident -- Phase 2 (the slot-walk) must run the submit\'s own allocation counter to derive it. (b) loc_8C1216C0 (the proj-matrix SETUP that BUILDS M1/M2 from camera params) is not yet transpiled (stubbed); M1/M2 read resident. Transpiling it would make the camera matrices themselves code-derived (only needed for objects whose camera state isn\'t in a dump).',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:render_replica_phase2_slotwalk SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-12',
  statement='RENDER-REPLICA PHASE 2 DONE (2026-06-12, branch feat/render-replica-experiment, tools/render-replica-poc/). The render ROOT loc_8c0308c2 (Render_sprites, bank03:1200) is transpiled (gen_walker_root.c -> render_sprites_0308c2), so render_frame(ram16mb) walks the ENTIRE slot table and renders EVERY on-screen BODY object via the Phase-1 render_object_full chain. SLOT-WALK (byte-exact hand-port, every line cites a bank03 disasm line): 16 layers; count u8 @ 0x8C2895E0+L (loop end r8=base+0x10, bank03:1214); node ptrs u32 @ 0x8C287DE0 + L*0x180 + i*4 (bank03:1213/1225-1226); per node category byte @+0x3 (bank03:1227). *** BRANCH TRUTH (corrects the task framing): tst r0,r0; bf -> cat!=0 = EFFECT (loc_8c030af8); FALL-THROUGH cat==0 = BODY (loc_8c03093c). So category==0 => BODY, category!=0 => EFFECT (confirmed vs loc_8c030af8 itself which re-reads +0x3 and only processes 0<cat<5, bank03:1538-1552; and re-catalog 00-README category@+0x3). The +0x12C visibility/cull gate lives INSIDE loc_8c03093c (bank03:1287-1290: read +0x12C; if 0 -> bra skip), honored by render_object_full (which runs render_object_setup_03093c first). CURSOR-ALLOCATION CLOSURE (the load-bearing Phase-2 piece, closes Phase-1 open-seam a): the per-object rectab base is COMPUTED by running the engine\'s own allocation cursor, NOT RAM-discovered. The chain (3 confirming disasm sites): arena base *(0x8C1F9D94)=16|400 (frame parity, frame-setup loc_8c033950 bank03:8460-8469); per-object setup loc_8c033b0a deposits node+0xDC = *(0x8C1F9D98) (the running prefix cursor, bank03:8751-8772) then advances *(0x8C1F9D98) += record_tile_count (loc_8c033d44 bank03:8057-8059); the body render walker loc_8c0344d4 computes the per-tile alloc index *r13 = node+0xDC + *(0x8C1F9D94) + k (bank03:10325-10330, +1/tile at 10752); the submit loc_8C1244B0 maps rectab[idxtab[*r13]] (bank12:9853-9874, the direct idxtab[*r13] path; loc_8c034944 pool confirms the walker\'s submit = loc_8C1244B0). => for body object n, tile k: idxtab_index = prefix_sum(n) + arena_base + k where prefix_sum(n) = sum of ntiles(0..n-1). render_frame keeps a running_cursor (seeded 0, advanced by each object\'s emitted tile count in slot-walk order) and ASSERTS computed running_cursor == the engine\'s resident node+0xDC per object -- the proof the cursor generalizes Phase-1\'s single RAM-discovered base. VALIDATION (cid23/P2C1 Cable, the only body in the matched dump\'s slot table, L06): (1) the transpiled slot-walk enumerated the body and rendered 9 tiles; (2) computed running-prefix (0) == engine resident node+0xDC (0) OK; (3) PCW/ISP/TSP/TCW 9/9 byte-exact vs the engine TA; (4) corners 9/9 at 0.0000px vs the engine TA; (5) rendered through the gold-standard pvr2-renderer = 100.0000% pixel match (307200/307200, 0 diff px, maxDelta=0) vs the engine bodies. MULTI-OBJECT scope: the matched dump (mc_ram_dump.bin/mc_engine_ta.bin) is a SINGLE-character-on-screen frame -- only cid23 is in the slot table (the other 5 slots inactive) and the engine TA has only 9 pal-24 sprites, so the byte-exact diff covers ONE real body; the multi-object cursor advance is proven by (a) computed prefix == resident node+0xDC, and (b) a SYNTHETIC 2-body test (render_frame_test.c) confirming object 2\'s base = object 1\'s base + ntiles(object1) (arena=16: baseA=16, baseB=25, final cursor=14 for 9+5) per the ROM formula. The verification: for cid23 node+0xDC=0, arena=16, *r13[k]=16+k, idxtab[16..24]=9..17 (contiguous), rectab[9..17] all pal24/fmt5 = EXACTLY Phase-1\'s RAM-discovered base=9 -- now derived by following node+0xDC + cursor + idxtab indirection. WASM: render_frame.wasm/render_frame.mjs (build_wasm_frame.sh, emcc) exports render_frame_ta(ram16mb,out_ta,cap)/render_frame_body_count()/render_frame_quad_count(); fed the LIVE 16MB RAM dump (NOT a baked image) it enumerates the body via the slot-walk and emits 9 body tiles, params 9/9 + corners 9/9 == native (verify_frame_wasm.mjs). web/render-replica/index.html updated to call render_frame (whole-scene). LEFT FOR PHASE 3: the effect path loc_8c030af8 (cat 1..4 satellites: capes/projectiles/effects, stubbed render_effect_030af8) + HUD + stage.',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:render_replica_readset SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-12',
  statement='RENDER-REPLICA PHASE 4a (LIVE-WIRE read-set) DONE (2026-06-12, branch feat/render-replica-experiment, tools/render-replica-poc/). The EXACT per-render_frame guest-RAM read-set is DERIVED (not guessed) and PARTITIONED into STATIC (ship once) vs DYNAMIC (ship per frame) with UNCLASS=0 -- the completeness proof: every byte render_frame reads falls in exactly one band. METHOD: trace_readset.c (-include sh4ctx_trace.h, a read-recording drop-in for sh4ctx.h) runs ONE render_frame over the matched dump (_ryu_capture/mc_ram_dump.bin, the Phase-2 byte-exact frame), records every guest-RAM read (addr,size), coalesces into [start,end) regions, classifies each by a cited band table, and asserts UNCLASS bytes == 0 (achieved). READ-SET (476 read events, single-Cable frame): DYNAMIC = slot-table count 0x8C2895E0(0x10) + slot ptrs 0x8C287DE0(16*0x180) + 6 char structs 0x8C268340(6*0x5A4) + arena ctrl 0x8C1F9D80(0x20) + tile-descriptor scratch 0x8C1F9F9C(0x200, ROLLING per-frame per body_walker_tiling) + camera mats 0x8C2D6AD8(0xC0) + camZ block 0x8C26A510(0x40) + GameGlobalPointer 0x8C26823C(4) + global-accum struct *(GGP)=0x8C268240(0x40, +0x24 RMW per object, loc_8c034bea) + per-char render-param 0x8C26A974(0x100) + rectab/idxtab ptr pair 0x8C2DAD30(0x40) + render-mode word 0x8C2AA4C4 + idxtab *(0x8C2DAD3C)(0x2000) + rectab *(0x8C2DAD4C)(0x8000). STATIC = GFX1 node+0x15C(0x20000) + GFX2 node+0x160(0x20000) per active body + VRAM(8MB part pixels) + PVR regs(0x8000). PoC r15 stack 0x0C480000 = SCRATCH (caller-owned, excluded). KEY CLASSIFICATIONS (cited): idxtab/rectab are DYNAMIC (per-frame allocation tables, re_kb submit_rectab_alloc_index/submit_arena_base); 0x8C1F9F9C is DYNAMIC not static (rolling per-frame scratch, re_kb body_walker_tiling 2026-06-12 correction); GFX1/GFX2+VRAM are STATIC (load-time char art, frame-invariant). The unclassified read 0x8C268264 was resolved to *(GameGlobalPointer)+0x24 (the global-accum RMW) and folded into DYNAMIC -> UNCLASS=0. BANDWIDTH (the render-replica thesis number): TOUCHED dynamic = 681 bytes/frame (single body, lower bound); WHOLE-REGION dynamic (multi-character-safe, ship-everything v1) ~58 KB/frame dominated by rectab(32KB)+idxtab(8KB)+char structs(8.5KB)+slot ptrs(6KB), ~3.5 MB/s @60fps raw; with per-region dirty-diff (v2) collapses toward the ~681B touched floor (~0.04 MB/s = GSTA-scale) -- proving the feed is STATE-sized not pixel-sized. CAPTURE: headless MAPLECAST_REPLICA_RECORD=<N> (+optional _PATH) in mc_oracle_charPassCapture (modeled on MAPLECAST_DUMP_RAM, same mem/vram/pvr/thd plumbing), READ-ONLY (addrspace + array reads), determinism-safe, in-match gate 0x8C289624, writes static-block once then N per-frame dynamic+engineTA records to /dev/shm/mc_render_rec.bin, closes+latches off. COMPLETENESS GUARANTEE: render_frame(static@f0 + dynamic@fK) reproduces the engine frame-K TA byte-exact iff every byte render_frame reads is in static union dynamic -- which UNCLASS=0 proves; frame-0 self-consistency already 100% in Phase 2; the dynamic set covers everything that changes frame-to-frame (char pos/scale/sprite_id/+0xDC, camera mats, alloc cursor/idxtab/rectab, descriptor scratch -- all cited write-sites). LEFT FOR 4b/4c: page replays the recording -> motion (validate per-frame vs embedded engine TA); same dynamic stream over live WS (v1 raw -> v2 dirty-diff).',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:render_replica_sh4_little_endian SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-12',
  statement='MVC2\'s SH4 runs LITTLE-ENDIAN; the prod RAM dump (mem_b) is verbatim LE (a node+0x34 posX value reads as dump bytes 55555543 = LE 0x43555555 = 213.33). The render-replica PoC\'s sh4ctx.h was originally BIG-ENDIAN accessors + a byteswapped image -- a DOUBLE inversion that cancelled for 32/16-bit ALIGNED reads (so the walker passed) but CORRUPTED sub-word BYTE reads (node+0x12c entry guard, node+0x5d zoom guard, the descriptor bytes read via mov.b). Phase 1 needs those byte reads (loc_8c03093c\'s node+0x12c/0x5d guards), so sh4ctx.h was switched to LITTLE-ENDIAN accessors + a VERBATIM dump copy (build_image_dump.py be32/bef32 flipped to LE; build_image_full.py copies verbatim). Re-verified: the proven walker test (FULL-WALKER NUMERIC) stays 9/9 @ 0.00px with the negative control correctly failing; leaf 21/21, transform 18/18 unchanged. CITE: tools/render-replica-poc/sh4ctx.h, build_image_dump.py, build_image_full.py.',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:render_replica_ta_emit SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-12',
  statement='OPTION C STAGE 2 CLOSED (tools/render-replica-poc/ step [6/6], test_ta_emit.c + gen_submit.py). The lift-to-C chain now emits the GAME-NATIVE PVR TA command stream: WALKER loc_8c0344d4 (per-tile top-left screenX/Y, proven 9/9 @0.00px) -> TRANSFORM loc_8c1216c0 (RESIDENT: world->screen result is already node+0xE0/E4 anchor + node+0xEC/F0 scale; the RAM dump byte-exactly holds 533.86 / 5over3 / 15over7, so the 9850-insn ftrv tree need not be re-run for a resident object) -> SUBMIT loc_8C1244B0->loc_8C124AB0 (4 corners = anchor + R(angle).(scale*unit_offset); body angle=0 => axis-aligned, confirmed vs probe_body_uv.json). RESULT for cid23 frame 10766: 9 quads, corner extent ROM-exact (tile size m=descriptor byte[0], W=m*scaleX H=m*scaleY; maxerr=0.0000), written to ta_buffer.bin (1472 bytes / 46 TA params) and ROUND-TRIPPED through the real web/webgpu/ta-parser.mjs (verify_ta.mjs) -> 9 opaque textured polys / 36 vertices, corners byte-exact. NEW OPCODES added to codegen.py for the matrix/submit core: ftrv (4x4 XF-bank * FV column-major, models xf[16] separate from fr[16]), frchg (FR<->XF swap + FPSCR.FR toggle), fschg (FPSCR.SZ toggle), fsca (sin/cos from 16-bit angle), shad/shar/shll16/shll8/shlr16/shlr8/shlr2/shlr, xor/not/cmp/hs/cmp/hi/pref, sign-extended cmp/eq #imm, fcnvsd/ds identity. FP/bank subtlety: ftrv reads the XF (secondary) bank that frchg makes active for the projection matrix; body path never flips FR/SZ (axis-aligned single-precision) so the walker+corner chain needs no bank routing, but the opcodes are in place for the full tree. TA buffer format = standard LE PowerVR2 32-byte params: Polygon-param(paraType4: PCW/ISP/TSP/TCW) + 4 Vertex-params(paraType7: x/y/z/u/v/col, strip TL,TR,BL,BR, last=EndOfStrip) + EndOfList(paraType0). x/y=final screen px (exact), z=1; tcw is a documented sel-keyed PLACEHOLDER (this dump has no GFX1 pixels; body sel pixels come from CHARQ/BODYCAP) and u/v unit[0,1] (harness applies real per-sel UV from probe_body_uv.json) -- geometry is exact, tex-binding is the documented seam. NOT deployed (offline harness commit only). OPEN: (1) the full ftrv matrix tree loc_8c1216c0 transpile for objects whose node+0xE0/E4 is not dump-resident; (2) the submit tcw/tsp/pcw bit-assembly (loc_8c1246da..loc_8c1248ea) transpile to derive real PVR control words instead of placeholders.',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:ryu_sid63_two_part_is_correct_not_wire_gap SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-11',
  statement='ROOT CAUSE of Ryu (cid0) rendering only 2 emitter parts vs ~20 TA-truth tiles = NOT a wire-field gap and NOT a multi-object body. The OFFLINE EXTRACTION IS CORRECT: PL00 GFX2 (GFX_DATA_01.BIN, 441 cells) cell index 63 genuinely has exactly 2 records [sel261 ddx33 ddy3 flags0 ; sel260 ddx-2 ddy91 flags0] (raw BIN parse, no guard fired since cnt=2). sel260 = a 64x128-native COMPACT single-texture body, sel261 = 8x8. The cnt>64 guard in rip_gfx2_assembly.read_cells did NOT drop anything. The emitter reproduced cell 63 faithfully. PROOF the model is sound: same dump PL08 cid8 sid53 -> GFX2 cell 53 has 13 records == 13 emitter parts, pixel-matches TA; and earlier frames Magneto cid44 sid127 -> 20 parts, healthy. The discrepancy is specific to sid63. WHY THE TA HAS 20 TILES: the live engine drew the body from a DIFFERENT, multi-tile sprite_id than the 63 that GSTA read from char+0x144 at capture time. Evidence: (a) the compact body sel260 spans screen X195-302 Y232-506 and the 20-tile TA body spans X167-304 Y232-506 = SAME body region, two representations (compact 2-part vs detailed ~20-tile) — they are the same pose drawn at different detail, not body+separate-arm-object; (b) no single Ryu GFX2 cell reproduces the TA tile multiset {8x32x32 + 8x16x16 + 3x8x8 + a 126x5}, and an inverse pen-search over all 441 cells tops out at 9/20 matched tiles — so the TA body is NOT cell 63 AND the captured sid does not index the detailed body. (c) 39/441 Ryu cells are 1-2-record compact cells; cell 63 is one; the multi-tile idle/body poses live in the 8-19 record cells. CONCLUSION: this is a SPRITE_ID CAPTURE/FRESHNESS issue (char+0x144 held a compact-cell sid 63 while the engine\'s body-walker loc_8c0344d4 indexed GFX2 with a different, detailed sid), NOT a missing GSTA wire field and NOT a multi-object body. The operator\'s \'missing wire fields\' instinct is NOT the answer for THIS defect.',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:sprite_id_0x144_is_authoritative_cell_selector SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-11',
  statement='ROM-CONFIRMED (read-the-ROM): the live body walker selects the GFX2 cell EXCLUSIVELY from char+0x144 (sprite_id), the SAME field GSTA already ships. Trace loc_8c0344d4 entry bank03:10232-10243 -- r0=0x160 (loc_8c0345fc), r4=Dat_GFX2=deref(player+0x160), then \'add 0xE4,r0\' where 0xE4 is a SIGN-EXTENDED imm8 (=-0x1C) so r0=0x160-0x1C=0x144 (NOT 0x244), reads deref(player+0x144) as a 32-bit word, masks &0x7FFF (loc_8c0345fe strips bit15), shll2, cell=GFX2+deref(GFX2+idx*4) (10241-10243); u16@cell=record count (10244); count x 8-byte recs [dx s16][dy s16][pal/flags u16][sel u16=read_u16(r11+6)] with a cumulative pen. Alternate routine loc_8c0348c8 (bank03:10800) has a BYTE-IDENTICAL selector sequence (0x160 / add 0xE4 / &0x7FFF), indexes the SAME GFX2 table, and differs ONLY in the bank11 world-transform helper (loc_8c11e2e0 / loc_8c11e860 vs loc_8c11e460). Caller loc_8c034bea (bank03:11259) reads 0x144, returns without drawing if ==0xFF, and routes on bit15 (0x8000): set -> loc_8c0348c8, clear -> loc_8c0344d4. bit15 is a TRANSFORM-VARIANT flag stripped by &0x7FFF before cell indexing -- NOT a second cell table, NOT a LOD field. char+0x244 (pl_mem unk244 \'float\') is unrelated. The anim tick loc_8c034dee (bank03:11567) writes 0x144 as byte+4 of the 20-byte keyframe copied from deref(0x154) into player+0x140 (loc_8c1294c8 duff copy), so 0x144 == deref(0x154)+4 within a frame. VERDICT: the wrong-pose bug is NOT a wrong wire field. It is a CAPTURE-FRESHNESS / SAMPLE-ORDERING issue: GSTA must sample 0x144 in the SAME engine phase the render walk runs (post-anim-tick, after the SH4 frame completes in serverPublish), and ship it MASKED &0x7FFF with bit15 carried as a transform flag. Server fix in maplecast_gamestate.cpp: keep reading 0x144 (correct field, line 45/188), sample it post-frame not mid-frame, apply &0x7FFF for the GFX2 index, carry bit15 separately, and (if any residual doubt) confirm with a single READ-ONLY Oracle probe at PC 0x8C0344D4 dumping the resolved index (r0 after the \'and\') vs char+0x144.',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:sprite_id_bit15_dispatch SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-12',
  statement='sprite_id bit15 (0x8000) @ char/node +0x144 is a PER-FRAME RENDER-PATH DISPATCH bit, NOT a horizontal-flip flag. loc_8c034bea: bit15 CLEAR -> loc_8c0344d4 (standard assembly); bit15 SET -> loc_8c0348c8 (per-part-SCALED assembly). BOTH mask sid&0x7FFF and index the SAME GFX2 cell table @node+0x160. So 0x8001->index 1, 0x8002->index 2, drawn with the scaled-part assembler. Horizontal flip is the SEPARATE facing field @+0x110 (setter loc_8c0d97ee) plus the PER-RECORD flag 0x4000 inside each 8-byte cell record (bank03:10477). The web client treating bit15 as xflip is WRONG.',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:submit_isp_depthmode SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-12',
  statement='SUBMIT ISP DepthMode finalize (render-replica renderer-input). The resident per-tile PVR poly-param template (rectab[idxtab[sel]] at rectab+0x04) holds ISP = 0x00000000 = DepthMode 0 (\'Never\') for the body. pvr2-renderer.mjs:234 SKIPS opaque polys with DepthMode==0 -> the body would draw 0 pixels if fed the resident ISP verbatim. The engine\'s OWN TA carries ISP = 0x80000000 = DepthMode 4 (\'Greater/Equal\') for the same polys -> the engine FINALIZES the depth bits downstream of the resident template (between the submit\'s verbatim copy and the actual TA emit). For the off-SH4 replica, finalize the body\'s ISP depth bits to DepthMode=4 (0x80000000) when emitting the TA. Geometry/TCW/TSP stay bit-exact; only the ISP depth nibble is finalized. Caught only by diffing the transpiled output vs the engine\'s real TA (mc_engine_ta.bin).',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:submit_rectab_alloc_index SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-12',
  statement='SUBMIT TEXTURE-PARAM INDEXING -- CORRECTED. The body submit loc_8C1244B0 indexes rectab by *r13 = the per-tile ALLOCATION index the walker writes at stack[r15+0x2C], NOT by sprite_id/sel. The earlier build_image_dump.py used idxtab[sel*2] (e.g. sel1264 -> idxtab[1264]=986 -> rectab[986], pal=28, texaddr 0x61A720) which is the WRONG entry -- it decoded plausibly but did NOT match the engine TA (pal=24, texaddr 0x415400). That mismatch is exactly why the texture params were PINNED to mc_engine_ta.bin. The REAL mapping: the engine allocated this object\'s 9 tiles a CONTIGUOUS run rectab[9..17] (= idxtab[16..24]), already FULLY FINALIZED in the STARTRENDER dump (PCW=A2000009/ISP=80000000/TSP=949004D2/TCW=2B082A80.. all byte-exact == engine TA, pal=24 baked). Walker tile k (emission order) -> rectab[base+k] 1:1 (verified: bottom-left anchors byte-identical, X-corners 463/516/569). base=9 is RAM-discoverable as the unique contiguous run of >=ntile pal-bank/fmt5 rectab entries. So the texture params read straight from the resident rectab[base+k] -- no engine-TA needed. CITE: marvelous2 bank12 loc_8C124520 (r8=idxtab[*r13]) / loc_8C124534 (rectab+r8*0x20); bank03 loc_8c034864 (submit call, r4=r15+0x2C) / loc_8c034744 region (walker stack record). Supersedes the build_image_dump.py STALE-pointer comment.',
  status='confirmed';

UPSERT finding:submit_tcw_resident SET
  confidence='high',
  date='2026-06-12',
  statement='MVC2 body-part TCW/TSP/PCW/ISP are RESIDENT deposited fields, NOT computed in the submit. Chain: sel -> r8=idxtab[sel] (idxtab=*(0x8C2DAD3c)) -> rectab[r8*0x20] (rectab=*(0x8C2DAD4c)), TCW@+0x0C / TSP@+0x08 / ISP@+0x04 / PCW@+0x00 (canonical PVR poly-param). TCW = live DM00 texaddr + PixelFmt(5 PAL4) + PalSelect. The ONLY computed step = PalSelect OR at loc_8c124a82: TCW=(TCW&0xF81FFFFF)|(palbank<<21). UV per body tile = [0,1] if part fills the 8<<TexU texture tile, else [0,m/tile]. VALIDATED bit-exact: render-replica-poc test_ta_emit.exe cid23 frame10766 9/9 quads emitted TCW==engine resident TCW, TSP 9/9, round-tripped through real ta-parser.mjs.',
  status='confirmed';

